// Workspace file for the repository root.
//
// The Go module lives in backend/, not at the repository root, because this
// repo also holds the Next.js web app, the Tauri POS and the design docs.
// Without this file gopls opens the root as an "AdHoc" view, sees no module,
// and cannot resolve symbols inside backend/ — which silently disables Serena's
// symbolic tools even though the language server appears to start correctly.
//
// It also gives a home to the desktop and web tooling later without another
// round of editor configuration.

go 1.26

// Repeated from backend/go.mod, because in a workspace THIS file decides the
// toolchain and the module’s own directive is ignored. Without this line the
// pin backend/go.mod describes silently does not happen: a build here used
// whatever Go the machine had — 1.26.5, carrying the four stdlib advisories
// (crypto/tls, net/http, encoding/xml, encoding/asn1) that 1.26.6 fixes and
// that CI pins 1.26.6 to avoid. The comment in go.mod claimed the local build
// and CI were on the same compiler; they were not.
toolchain go1.26.6

use ./backend
